 {"version_id": "struct-05", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Require completion claims to carry validation evidence", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient completion or validation of final changes", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["sympy__sympy-20154", "sympy__sympy-15011", "django__django-11001", "django__django-11910"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "patchwork/common/multiturn_strategy/planning_strategy.py", "find": "class ExecutionResult(BaseModel):\n    json_data: str\n    message: str\n    is_completed: bool", "replace": "class ExecutionResult(BaseModel):\n    json_data: str\n    message: str\n    is_completed: bool\n    validation_evidence: str = \"\"\n\n    @property\n    def completion_is_credible(self) -> bool:\n        return not self.is_completed or bool(self.validation_evidence.strip())"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.62, "reasoning_soundness": 0.58, "execution_accuracy": 0.45, "output_integrity": 0.61}, "aggregate": 0.565, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-20154", "score": 0.77}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15011", "score": 0.75}, {"instance_id": "django__django-11001", "score": 0.19}, {"instance_id": "django__django-11910", "score": 0.18}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0175, "why": "Requiring validation evidence is the strongest direct improvement to completion reporting and raises output integrity. However, evidence is only checked for non-emptiness rather than substantive correctness, and gating completion claims can reduce execution throughput or reject otherwise valid results."}
+{"version_id": "struct-06", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Reject malformed structured execution payloads at the result boundary", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient completion or validation of final changes", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["sympy__sympy-20154", "sympy__sympy-15011", "django__django-11001", "django__django-11910"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "patchwork/common/multiturn_strategy/planning_strategy.py", "find": "from pydantic import BaseModel", "replace": "from pydantic import BaseModel, field_validator"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.6, "reasoning_soundness": 0.55, "execution_accuracy": 0.43, "output_integrity": 0.5}, "aggregate": 0.52, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-20154", "score": 0.75}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15011", "score": 0.73}, {"instance_id": "django__django-11001", "score": 0.15}, {"instance_id": "django__django-11910", "score": 0.14}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": -0.0275, "why": "The shown change only imports a validator and does not demonstrate an actual payload validator or enforcement path. It therefore provides little functional benefit, while introducing possible Pydantic-version compatibility risk and leaving completion and validation failures largely unchanged."}
+{"version_id": "struct-07", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Repository-aware execution contract", "target_failure_mode": "Repository- and issue-type generalization failure", "expected_dimension": "target_alignment", "evidence_instance_ids": ["sympy__sympy-20154", "sympy__sympy-15011", "django__django-11001", "django__django-11910"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "patchwork/common/multiturn_strategy/agentic_strategy.py", "find": "                \"Work repository-first: inspect the target repository's conventions, neighboring implementations, tests, and supported versions before editing. Prefer the smallest compatible patch and verify it with focused tests.\"\n", "replace": "                \"Work repository-first: first identify the repository, framework, version constraints, issue category, relevant subsystem, neighboring implementations, and applicable tests. Adapt terminology and conventions to that repository rather than relying on generic solutions. Prefer the smallest compatible patch and verify it with focused tests.\"\n"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.66, "reasoning_soundness": 0.6, "execution_accuracy": 0.49, "output_integrity": 0.55}, "aggregate": 0.575, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-20154", "score": 0.8}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15011", "score": 0.78}, {"instance_id": "django__django-11001", "score": 0.21}, {"instance_id": "django__django-11910", "score": 0.19}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0275, "why": "The repository-first contract directly improves issue and subsystem targeting, with modest reasoning and execution benefits. Its broad, partially truncated wording is less operational than an explicit reconnaissance or execution protocol, so gains remain limited."}
